description: Follow the QFBMS charge-only build plan and mechanical constraints
alwaysApply: true
---

Read README.md, PLAN.md, and DESIGN_RULES.md at the repository root before design work.
The active board is qfbms32.kicad_pcb: a 32s charge-only BMS, with no discharge-protection requirement.
Preserve placed connectors and balance/heatsink-related parts, including R_B1–R_B33.
Keep the BQ monitors approximately in place; limited local movement and justified support-circuit changes are allowed during electrical work.
Use docs/FIRMWARE_INTERFACE.md and the supplied firmware/package as the software compatibility baseline, and TI guidance for electrical requirements.
Use _reference/user_photos/ for placement. Resolve the C_F back-side exception under DESIGN_RULES.md before moving those parts.
docs/history/ contains superseded proposals, not active instructions. Do not run archived generators or alter the electrical design during documentation or repository maintenance.
